-- title:
--   Möbius-weighted fixed-coset count equals count of conjugating elements
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite group and let $\sigma,\tau \in G$; write $n = \operatorname{orderOf}\sigma$. For each divisor $f$ of $n$ consider the cyclic subgroup $\langle \sigma^{n/f}\rangle$ generated by $\sigma^{n/f}$ (in Lean, `Subgroup.zpowers`, the group of integer powers), the left coset space $G/\langle\sigma^{n/f}\rangle$ with its natural left $G$-action, and the set of cosets $x$ fixed by $\tau$, i.e. $\tau\cdot x = x$; let its cardinality be measured by `Set.ncard`. The assertion is the identity in $\mathbb{Z}$
--   $$\sum_{f \mid n} \mu\!\left(\frac{n}{f}\right)\, f \cdot \#\{x \in G/\langle\sigma^{n/f}\rangle : \tau\cdot x = x\} \;=\; \#\{g \in G : \exists\, k \in \mathbb{N},\ \gcd(k,n)=1 \text{ and } g\,\sigma^{k}\,g^{-1} = \tau\},$$
--   where the sum runs over the divisors of $n$ in the sense of `Nat.divisors`, $\mu$ is the Möbius function, and the right-hand count is again an `ncard`, coerced to $\mathbb{Z}$. Thus the Möbius combination of the fixed-coset counts, weighted by the orders $f$ of the subgroups, counts exactly those $g \in G$ that conjugate some generator $\sigma^{k}$ of $\langle\sigma\rangle$ to $\tau$. No hypothesis beyond finiteness of $G$ is imposed.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic core of Frobenius's density theorem: the inclusion–exclusion identity that converts counts of degree-one primes in intermediate fields (fixed cosets for a Frobenius element) into counts of elements conjugating a generator of $\langle\sigma\rangle$ to $\tau$. It is used in the derivation of the Frobenius density statement from the degree-one asymptotics, [`FrobeniusDensity.statement_of_degOneAsymptotic`](thm.html#FrobeniusDensity.statement_of_degOneAsymptotic), and in the Dirichlet-density computation for towers with $\operatorname{orderOf}$ equal to eight used in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the argument. The collapse of the inner Möbius sum relies on [`ArithmeticFunction.sum_moebius_filter_dvd`](thm.html#ArithmeticFunction.sum_moebius_filter_dvd), which evaluates $\sum_{f \mid n}\mu(n/f)\,[\,m \mid f\,]$ as the indicator of $m = n$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FrobeniusDensity_weight_eq.lean

import Mathlib.NumberTheory.ArithmeticFunction.Moebius
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.QuotientGroup.Basic
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement
import Mathlib.Data.Set.Card

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped Classical in

theorem FrobeniusDensity.weight_eq {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] (σ τ : G) :
    ∑ f ∈ (orderOf σ).divisors,
        (ArithmeticFunction.moebius (orderOf σ / f)) *
          ((f : ℤ) * ({x : G ⧸ Subgroup.zpowers (σ ^ (orderOf σ / f)) | τ • x = x}.ncard : ℤ))
      = ({g : G | ∃ k : ℕ, k.Coprime (orderOf σ) ∧ g * σ ^ k * g⁻¹ = τ}.ncard : ℤ) := by sorry
